{
  "notes": [
    "Steel tubes (mitcad#873): Mitcad's own parts of the standards' sizes, no supplier. Each is one design whose rows are its outside size x wall thickness, cut to length in the BUILD tab.",
    "Round and square tubes: EN 10219-2 cold-formed welded hollow sections (circular up to 323.9, square up to 300x300), the round tubes' outside diameters of EN 10220 series 1. The square tubes' corners have the standard's radii for calculation: T <= 6 mm outer 2.0 T, inner 1.0 T; 6 < T <= 10 mm 2.5 T and 1.5 T; T > 10 mm 3.0 T and 2.0 T.",
    "Furniture tubes: EN 10305-5:2016 Table 6, the square sizes of welded cold-sized square precision tubes (E195, E220, E235; +CR1). Corners: T <= 2.5 mm outer 0.5 T with a sharp inner corner; T 3 to 4 mm outer 1.75 T, inner 0.75 T. Tolerances: the side as each size gives; the wall T <= 1.5 mm +-0.15 mm, over 1.5 mm +-0.1 T or +-0.35 mm, whichever is smaller.",
    "Density 7850 kg/m3: the sections are modelled exactly, so a row's mass per metre is the standard's (CHS 48.3x3.2 3.56 kg/m, SHS 40x40x3 3.30 kg/m, 30x30x1.5 1.34 kg/m).",
    "Rectangular tubes (mitcad#892): EN 10219-2 cold-formed rectangular hollow sections from 40x20 to 400x300, with the square tubes' corner radii (RHS 100x50x4 8.59 kg/m); EN 10305-5:2016 Table 6, the rectangular sizes of the furniture tubes from 20x10 to 120x60, with their corners and tolerances (40x20x2 1.75 kg/m). Width x height, the width the longer side.",
    "Stainless tubes (mitcad#892): EN ISO 1127 Table 3, the outside diameters and wall thicknesses of austenitic stainless steel tubes up to 323.9 mm (the sizes of EN 10216-5 seamless and EN 10217-7 welded tubes), at the standard's conventional density 7970 kg/m3 (42.4x2 2.02 kg/m)."
  ],
  "categories": [{"id": "steel-tubes", "name": "Tubes"}],
